# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.5.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-IMAGESIZE-17295814:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Only reachable through metro@0.83.3's own bundler internals
          (image-size is imported directly by Metro's source, build-time
          only — never shipped in the app bundle). The patched release is
          an ESM-only 2.x major with a different export shape that Metro's
          code isn't written against; forcing it risks breaking asset
          dimension probing on every build. Exploitation would require
          feeding a crafted malicious image into a trusted local build,
          which isn't a realistic path here. Revisit once Expo/Metro bump
          their own image-size pin to 2.x.
        expires: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-IMAGESIZE-17295816:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Second CVE for the same image-size@1.2.1 finding via
          metro@0.83.3 — see SNYK-JS-IMAGESIZE-17295814 for the full
          rationale.
        expires: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-INFLIGHT-6095116:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Only reachable via glob@7.2.3, itself only pulled in by three
          devDependency-only chains: chromium-edge-launcher (Hermes
          debugger launcher), @react-native/codegen (build-time codegen),
          and babel-jest/test-exclude (Jest tooling). None of these ship
          in the app bundle. inflight's bug is a resource leak under
          sustained reuse in a long-running process — irrelevant to
          short-lived local dev/build/test runs. No patched inflight
          release was ever published; the real fix is those three
          packages migrating off glob@7 upstream, which isn't something
          an override here can safely force.
        expires: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
